    "name": "paper",
    "note": "Paper: btop's paper theme and the vim-paper palette it comes from (yorickpeterse/vim-paper: #F2EEDE, black ink, red #CC3E28, green #216609, blue #1E6FCC, yellow #B58900, purple #5C21A5, cyan #158C86, orange #A55000, the greys). Light is that palette as it is; its terminal is vim-paper's own sixteen. Dark is made here and keeps the character: the same warm paper hue, now the ground at low lightness, the paper colour as the ink, and the same sparse hues raised just enough to read on it. btop: the stock paper in light, custom in dark (monochrome boxes, as paper's are). Group tabs: the tab is the orange, a locked group's tab purple (light) / teal (dark). VS Code: the Paper extension (a5hk.paper) in light when it is installed, else Quiet Light; Kimbie Dark in dark.",
